From 8014cdb1df71c78c300a5a8b55bd368b3677e0cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: srtlab <gomezsteve1379@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 04:34:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] Safety gate: dealer-lockout 0xFF00 erase RID can't fire
 by accident
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

0xFF00 is the generic ISO-14229 firmware-erase RoutineIdentifier relabeled
'clear lockout counter', with an invented A5 5A C3 3C payload — neither
grounded in any extraction or bench capture. On a module where 0xFF00 means
erase, running it can brick the RFHUB.

The clear-lockout step now refuses to transmit unless the caller passes
acknowledgeEraseRisk:true; the harmless session/SA probe steps still run so
the operator still gets a diagnosis. RfhubTab gates the flag behind an explicit
window.confirm. Runtime-verified: without ack the 0x31/0xFF00 routine is never
sent; with ack it runs. Test updated to encode the contract + a refusal test.
